aner and exercises real code.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_last_balance_on_empty_ledger_returns_initial_value():\n    account = StubAccount(\"100\", \"Cash\")\n    initial = Balance(datetime.date(2021, 1, 1), Quantity(Decimal(\"1000\")))\n    ledger = Ledger(account, initial)\n\n    # `_last_balance` must fall back to the initial balance when there are no entries.\n    assert ledger._last_balance == Quantity(Decimal(\"1000\"))\n    assert ledger.entries == []\n```\n\nThis covers lines 127, 129, 130 (the try line, the except IndexError line, and the return).\n\n```python\ndef test_add_creates_entry_and_updates_balance():\n    account = StubAccount(\"100\", \"Cash\")\n    initial = Balance(datetime.date(2021, 1, 1), Quantity(Decimal(\"1000\")))\n    ledger = Ledger(account, initial)\n\n    posting1 = _make_posting(account, Direction.INC, Amount(Decimal(\"250\")))\n    entry1 = ledger.add(posting1)\n\n    # First entry: balance = initial + amount * direction (+1).\n    assert isinstance(entry1, LedgerEntry)\n    assert entry1.ledger is ledger\n    assert entry1.posting is posting1\n    assert entry1.balance == Quantity(Decimal(\"1250\"))\n    assert ledger.entries == [entry1]\n\n    posting2 = _make_posting(account, Direction.DEC, Amount(Decimal(\"400\")))\n    entry2 = ledger.add(posting2)\n\n    # Second entry: balance = last balance + amount * direction (-1).\n    assert entry2.balance == Quantity(Decimal(\"850\"))\n    assert ledger.entries == [entry1, entry2]\n```\n\nThis covers line 128 (return self.entries[-1].balance via `_last_balance` on second add) and lines 140, 143, 146 (add method).\n\nWait \u2014 line 128 is `return self.entries[-1].balance`. On the first `add`, `_last_balance` is called when entries is empty \u2192 IndexError path. On the second `add`, `_last_balance` is called when entries has one entry \u2192 line 128. \n\nAlso I should verify `_last_balance` directly after adding:\n\n```python\nassert ledger._last_balance == Quantity(Deci